Hi there,

I've gotten further in spork than I've ever got before, but given that 
even on vanilla I'm not a skilled player (only 2 ascensions), I'm really 
starting to feel that it's all too much for me.

I'm a human chaotic Barbarian, I've got Frost Brand, GDSM, shield of 
reflection, jumping boots, rings of free action and conflict, the castle 
wand (0:0), +3 leather gloves, cloak of displacement.

My intrinsics include sleep, fire, cold, poison and disintegration 
resistance, invisibility and see invisible, telepathy, speed, stealth, 
and teleportitis.

My AC is -11 -- not brilliant, I know, but I've only seen two scrolls of 
enchant armor, one of which I wrote with most of a magic marker. I'm 
also worried that my MC is too low at two.

I've got to the bottom of the quest, but Thoth Amon completely 
overwhelmed me with summoned monsters and I had to get out straight 
away. I dug to the Castle, cleaned it out (was hoping to kill everyone 
with the drawbridge but it got stuck somehow...)

There were a couple of titans between castle and medusa, who summoned 
enough MMFs that my brains got sucked once or twice. That was dumb of me 
:( luckily most of the "forgotten" items were easily remembered. It's 
quite amusing seeing "an uncursed -1 brass ring"...

I've just killed Medusa, and I'm on her level. It has a titan; I know I 
can take a titan out, but the ones I've taken out so far have been costly.

I don't have any ranged attacks; this is probably a mistake. I have a 
wand of light to make conflict work, and a can of grease to provide 
protection from eels and MMFs. (Clearly it doesn't protect enough.)

What should I do now? I can't wish using the castle wand because I lost 
my ?oCharging to a stupid typo. I can get back across Medusa by jumping, 
and perseus also had levitation boots.

Maybe I should try levitating and waiting til the Titan casts "fly" so I 
can kill him over water, safe from summoned monsters. Would that work?

Philip

